## Context

Over months of worktree-based development, ~50 remote branches have accumulated
on origin. Most are from merged PRs, closed experiments, or abandoned explorations.
They add noise to `git branch -a` and slow tab-completion.

## Actions

1. List all remote branches, cross-reference with merged PRs and closed tickets.
2. Delete branches whose PR is merged or whose work is abandoned.
3. Keep branches with open PRs or active worktrees.
4. Consider adding a post-merge hook or CI job to auto-delete branches after PR merge.

## Test

`git branch -r | wc -l` should drop from ~55 to <10.

## Exit criteria

Remote branches correspond only to open PRs or active work. No stale references.
